From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:48:00 -0500
Subject: feat: a bigger little window, at the size the user last gave one
 (S-407)

A link from another app opened in a window capped at 1000x700, about a third
of a laptop's screen at a high resolution (docs/features/little.md E1). It
still floats over the main window, centred on it as before, and is now four
fifths of that window's width and height, so it is about as big as a tab
while the browser shows round it. Once the user resizes a little window, the
next one opens at that size (stedding.little.width and .height), centred on
the window; the size one opened at, a peek's and a restored window's are
never kept. With no normal window on screen it is four fifths of the screen,
centred, where it had been uncentred (S-157). It is never under 400x300 nor
over the work area, and is moved onto the screen.

BrowserView reports each save of a window's placement; only a window
OpenLittleWindow opened, and only once its size differs from the one it
opened at, writes the size.

Why: the owner, 2026-11-03: on a laptop the little window took about a
third of the screen, where Arc's was as big as a real tab; a size the user
gives one is kept. Laid exactly over the page it read as part of the
browser, so it floats as before and only its size changed.
Removable when: never as a feature.
